Subject: use the POSIX command lookup in the OSTree GRUB helper
Source: Nex downstream patch for OSTree 2026.1
Upstream: not submitted; small portability fix for a retained integration file

The helper needs only the shell's standard command lookup. Avoid adding the
outside `which` program to every package or assembly that carries the script.

--- a/src/boot/grub2/grub2-15_ostree
+++ b/src/boot/grub2/grub2-15_ostree
@@ -20 +20 @@
-if ! which ostree >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
+if ! command -v ostree >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
